<section xml:id="sec-ws-01-onboarding">
  <title>Onboarding Practice</title>

  <objectives>
    <ul>
      <li>Recognize complete, incomplete, and multi-episode responses.</li>
      <li>Distinguish mathematical operations from controls.</li>
      <li>Identify criteria, inferential links, and judgments in responses.</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      <term>Instructions</term>. Read the review items below and complete the practice questions.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-ws-01-before">
    <title>Review</title>

    <p>
      Read the following sections to prepare for the practice questions:
      <ol>
        <li component="instructor"><p><xref ref="subsec-project-boundaries" text="title"/></p></li>
        <li component="instructor"><p><xref ref="subsec-ck-cent-operations-controls" text="title"/></p></li>
        <li><p><xref ref="subsec-episode-components" text="title"/></p></li>
        <li><p><xref ref="subsec-episode-explicit-implicit-absent" text="title"/></p></li>
        <li><p><xref ref="subsec-episode-complete-incomplete" text="title"/></p></li>
        <li>
          <p>
            <xref ref="subsec-episode-chained" text="title"/>,
            <xref ref="subsec-episode-independent" text="title"/>,
            <xref ref="subsec-episode-nested" text="title"/>
          </p>
        </li>
        <li component="instructor">
          <p>
            Worked Examples:
            <ul>
              <li><xref ref="example-one-complete" text="title"/></li>
              <li><xref ref="example-incomplete" text="title"/></li>
              <li><xref ref="example-chained" text="title"/></li>
            </ul>
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </p>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-ws-01-context">
    <title>Mathematical Context</title>

    <assemblage xml:id="assemblage-ws-01-question">
      <title>Training Question</title>

      <p>
          The reduced row echelon form of the augmented matrix of a system in the
          variables <m>x_1,x_2,x_3</m> is
          <md>
          \left[
          \begin{array}{ccc|c}
              1 &amp; 0 &amp; 2  &amp; 3\\
              0 &amp; 1 &amp; -1 &amp; 4\\
              0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0  &amp; 0
          \end{array}
          \right].
          </md>
          Is the system consistent? Does it have a unique solution? Identify the basic
          and free variables. Explain your reasoning.
      </p>

      <p>
          For this worksheet, use the following <xref ref="g-normative-reference" text="title"/>:
          <ul>
          <li>the system is consistent;</li>
          <li><m>x_1</m> and <m>x_2</m> are basic variables;</li>
          <li><m>x_3</m> is a free variable; and</li>
          <li>the system has infinitely many solutions and is not unique.</li>
          </ul>
      </p>
    </assemblage>
  </subsection>

  <worksheet xml:id="ws-01-practice">
    <title>Practice Questions</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-ws-01-operation-control">
      <title>Operation or Control</title>

      <statement>
        <p>
          Identify each operation and control structure in the following
          student responses.
        </p>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="7%"/>
          <col width="93%"/>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I row reduced the augmented matrix.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The bottom row is zero, so there are infinitely many solutions.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I counted two pivots.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>Column three has no pivot, so x3 is free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I solved for x1 and x2, and that left x3 free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          Note: An <term>operation</term> is a mathematical action performed on the system. A
          <term>control</term> is a decision or validation drawn from a feature.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R1</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="18%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="82%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I row reduced the augmented matrix.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I row reduced the augmented matrix.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Reason</p></cell>
            <cell><p>Row reduction is an action performed on the matrix; nothing is drawn based on it.</p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R2</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="18%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="82%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The bottom row is zero, so there are infinitely many solutions.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The bottom row is zero, so there are infinitely many solutions.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Reason</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>Since no action was performed, there is no operation.</p>
              <p>
                The feature: <q>The bottom row is zero</q> is used to justify 
                the decision: <q>there are infinitely many solutions</q>.
              </p>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R3</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="18%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="82%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I counted two pivots.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I counted two pivots.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Reason</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>
                Counting pivots is an action performed on the matrix. Although the
                resulting pivot count could later serve as a criterion, this statement
                does not use it to make a decision.
              </p>
            </cell>
          </row>

        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R4</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="18%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="82%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>Column three has no pivot, so x3 is free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>Column three has no pivot, so x3 is free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Reason</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>Since no action was performed, there is no operation.</p>
              <p>The criterion, <q>Column three has no pivot</q>, is used to come to the judgment that <q>x3 is free</q>.</p>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R5</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="18%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="82%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I solved for x1 and x2, and that left x3 free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Operation</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I solved for x1 and x2</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Control</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I solved for x1 and x2, and that left x3 free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>Reason</p></cell>
            <cell>
              <p>
                Solving for <q>x1</q> and <q>x2</q> is an operation. Using that
                outcome to decide that <q>x3 is free</q> is a control.
              </p>
              <p>
                The criterion here is not an observed feature such as a pivot count.
                Instead, it is the result of an operation: solving determined x1 and 
                x2 and left x3 unconstrained.
              </p>
              <p>
                Caution: <c>explicit</c>, <c>implicit</c>, and <c>absent</c> describe 
                the inferential link only. Do not describe a criterion as 
                <q>implicit</q>. A component is stated in the response, carried by 
                shown work, or missing.
              </p>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-ws-01-components">
      <title>Identify Episode Components</title>

      <statement>
        <p>
          For each response below, record:
          <ol>
            <li>the criterion <m>C</m>, copied <em>verbatim</em> from the student's words;</li>
            <li>the minimal link <m>I</m> sufficient to justify the step;</li>
            <li>the judgment <m>J</m>, copied <em>verbatim</em> from the student's words;</li>
            <li>whether the link status is <c>explicit</c>, <c>implicit</c>, or <c>absent</c>; and</li>
            <li>whether the episode is complete (yes=<c>1</c> or no=<c>0</c>).</li>
          </ol>
        </p>

        <tabular>
          <col width="7%"/>
          <col width="93%"/>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The augmented matrix has no [0 0 0 1] row, so the system is consistent.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The third column has no pivot. Therefore, x3 is free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>There are two pivots.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>x1 and x2 are basic variables.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The system has a free variable then the solution is not unique.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R6</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The system is consistent, and it has infinitely-many solns.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          (<em>Edited</em>) Note: Link status stays blank for an incomplete episode. 
          <c>absent</c> is reserved for when both a criterion and a judgment are 
          stated but no justification-link can be recovered; that episode remains
          <em>complete</em>. Separately, every <c>complete=0</c> row notes whether 
          an inferential marker (<q>so</q>, <q>because</q>, <q>therefore</q>) is 
          present.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R1</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="20%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="76%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The augmented matrix has no [0 0 0 1] row, so the system is consistent.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The augmented matrix has no [0 0 0 1] row</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p>The absence of a contradictory row means the system is consistent.</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>the system is consistent</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>explicit</c> (signaled by <q>so</q>)</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>1</c></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R2</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="20%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="76%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The third column has no pivot. Therefore, x3 is free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The third column has no pivot</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p>A variable whose column contains no pivot is free.</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>x3 is free</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>explicit</c> (signaled by <q>Therefore</q>)</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>1</c></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R3</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="20%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="76%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>There are two pivots.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>There are two pivots</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /> (leave blank; see the convention note below)</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>0</c> (no judgment; no inferential marker present)</p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          The response names a feature and stops. The feature is a possible
          criterion, but no judgment is drawn from it and no marker signals an
          inferential move. Do not supply the consequence the 
          <xref ref="assemblage-ws-01-question" text="custom">mathematical context</xref>
          makes obvious.
        </p>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R4</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="20%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="76%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>x1 and x2 are basic variables.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>x1 and x2 are basic variables</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>0</c> (no criterion; no inferential marker present)</p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          The sentence directly answers the identify-the-variables goal, so it is
          a bare answer: a judgment without a criterion. Do not import the missing
          criterion (<q>because columns one and two contain pivots</q>) from the
          normative reference.
        </p>

        <p>
          When deciding if a lone assertion belongs in the criterion or judgment 
          slot, apply the goal test:
          <ul>
            <li>if the assertion states one of the requested goals, make it a judgment.</li>
            <li>if it names a feature of the mathematical state, make it a criterion.</li>
            <li>if it gives an answer, but does not identify which goal, then give it a no episode row.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R5</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="20%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="76%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The system has a free variable then the solution is not unique.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The system has a free variable</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p>A free variable can take more than one value, producing more than one solution.</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>the solution is not unique</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>explicit</c> (signaled by <q>then</q>). Note, <q>then</q> is weaker than <q>so</q> or <q>therefore</q>, so <c>implicit</c> + <c>confidence=2</c> is a defensible alternative.</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>1</c></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R6</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="20%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="76%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R6</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The system is consistent, and it has infinitely-many solns.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The system is consistent</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>0</c> (no criterion; no inferential marker)</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_2 = C_2</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>I_2</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>J_2</m></p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>it has infinitely-many solns</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_2</m>-link status</p></cell>
            <cell><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p><m>e_2</m>-complete</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>0</c> (no criterion; no inferential marker)</p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          The <q>and</q> joins two assertions but is not an inferential marker: 
          neither claim is offered as a reason for the other.
          Each directly answers a goal (consistency; number of solutions), so the
          conservative segmentation records two bare answers: parallel judgments
          without criteria, non-interacting. Reading the second claim as
          following from the first would insert a marker the student did not
          write.
        </p>

        <p>
          Copy <q>infinitely-many solns</q> verbatim, abbreviation included;
          verbatim fields preserve the student's phrasing. Recognizing a
          defensible alternative segmentation is a signal to include a rationale
          for your choice and possibly downgrade the confidence (e.g.,
          <c>confidence=2</c>).
        </p>
      </solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-ws-01-screen-segment">
      <title>Screen and Segment Responses</title>

      <statement>
        <p>
          For each response:
          <ol>
            <li>state whether it contains analyzable mathematical justification;</li>
            <li>(<em>edited</em>) identify the defensible episodes and their components;</li>
            <li>(<em>edited</em>) mark each episode's completeness (yes=<c>1</c> or no=<c>0</c>); and</li>
            <li>state any <xref ref="sec-episode-relations" text="custom">relation</xref> among episodes.</li>
          </ol>
        </p>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="10%"/>
          <col width="80%"/>

          <row>
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>No.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>There is a free variable, so the solution cannot be unique.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R3</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>x1 = 3 - 2x3, x2 = 4 + x3.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>There are fewer pivots than variables, so x3 is free. Therefore, the solution is not unique.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R5</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>The last row is zero, so the system is consistent. Also, the third column has no pivot, so x3 is free.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>R6</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>I do not know.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          (<em>Edited</em>) Note: Screening asks only whether a response contains analyzable justification, not
          whether it is mathematically correct. Record the structure that is present; do not
          supply the argument the reference mathematics makes obvious.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R1</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="8%" halign="center"/>
          <col width="40%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="40%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R1</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><q>No.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(a)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p>No analyzable justification</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(b)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><mdash/></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(c)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><mdash/></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(d)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><mdash/></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          An answer is attempted, but what it refers to is unknown. Choosing one would add 
          information the response does not contain, so not even a bare-answer row is 
          recorded. In contrast, the statement <q>x1 and x2 are basic variables</q> in the 
          previous exercise is very likely a judgment from an implicit inference based on the
          form of the matrix system.
        </p>

        <p>
          Flag for review with a note rather than excluding since any contribution
          to <xref ref="g-goal-coverage" text="title"/> is handled in a later milestone, not here.
        </p>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R2</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="8%" halign="center"/>
          <col width="40%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="40%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R2</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><q>There is a free variable, so the solution cannot be unique.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(a)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p>Yes, there is analyzable justification</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(b)</p></cell>
            <cell><p><m>e_1 = C_1</m>:</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>There is a free variable</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell><p><m>J_1</m>:</p></cell>
            <cell><p><q>the solution cannot be unique</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(c)</p></cell>
            <cell><p><m>e_1</m>-complete:</p></cell>
            <cell><p><c>1</c></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(d)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><mdash /></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
