          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(c)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><mdash/></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(d)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><mdash/></p></cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>

        <p>
          Mathematical work is present, but it is not clear whether that
          is the student's answer or just work shown. So, avoid coding it
          as an episode. Because work is shown, flag it for review rather
          than excluding it outright.
        </p>
      </solution>

      <solution component="solution">
        <title>R4</title>

        <tabular valign="top">
          <col width="8%" halign="center"/>
          <col width="40%" halign="right"/>
          <col width="40%" halign="left"/>

          <row bottom="minor">
            <cell><p>R4</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p><q>There are fewer pivots than variables, so x3 is free. Therefore, the solution is not unique.</q></p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><p>(a)</p></cell>
            <cell colspan="2" halign="left"><p>Yes, there is analyzable justification</p></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
